    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A possible drainage issue is causing the waterslogged soil, which can lead to root rot. Inspect the roots by gently removing the plant from its pot and checking for softened, mushy, or blackened roots. If you find any of these signs, it's likely root rot, and repotting with fresh, well-draining soil might help. You can also try adding perlite or sand to your existing mix to improve drainage.",
